<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">The business has moved on, the website has not</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">New products, new markets, a different focus — and a website that still shows the company of five years ago. Prospects notice before they call. Some then do not call.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">In B2B, a website is not visited by one person but by several, each with different questions. The engineer looks for data and evidence. Purchasing looks for delivery capability and a contact. Management wants to know whether the company will still stand behind it in ten years.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A website that addresses all three in the same way addresses none of them properly.</p>
</section>

